1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,321
Step number one is the one that comes first and this is journaling.
第一步，也就是最先要做的，是写日记。

2
00:00:03,321 --> 00:00:08,521
Now listen I love commodified self care okay I love massages I love face masks.
听我说，我也喜欢商品化的自我照顾，好吗？我喜欢按摩，也喜欢面膜。

3
00:00:08,521 --> 00:00:12,480
But none of that is going to work unless it is combined with real introspection.
但她认为，如果不和真正的自我反思结合，这些都不会起作用。

4
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,470
And journaling is the thing that's going to help you with this.
而她认为，写日记就是能在这方面帮你的事情。

5
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:18,640
Before you incorporate all of these extra steps in your routine you need to grab out a piece of paper.
在把这些额外步骤加入日常之前，你得先拿出一张纸。

6
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:24,480
And you need to actually identify where you're struggling what your weaknesses are where you feel like you haven't healed yet.
认真找出：你在哪些地方感到困难，有什么弱点，以及哪些方面还觉得自己没有恢复。

7
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:26,280
How you think your happiness could be improved.
想想自己怎样才能更快乐。

8
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:30,920
And guess what the only person who knows the answers to any of those questions is you.
你知道吗？唯一知道这些问题答案的人，就是你自己。

9
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:36,161
But we aren't conscious about this because we're so consumed by the daily rush and responsibility of life.
但我们常常意识不到，因为生活中的匆忙和责任已经占满了我们的心思。

10
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:42,401
That we think that going on a quick walk or lighting a candle or having a bubble bath is supposed to make us relax.
所以我们以为，快走一小段、点支蜡烛，或者泡个泡泡浴，就应该能让我们放松。

11
00:00:42,401 --> 00:00:44,591
When we're never dealing with the problem at hand.
但她认为，我们其实始终没有处理眼前真正的问题。

12
00:00:44,601 --> 00:00:50,480
Like how have we gone this long thinking that everyone can have the same bubble bath routine and have everyone's problems fixed.
她反问，我们怎么会一直认为，所有人只要用同一套泡泡浴流程，就能解决各自的问题？

13
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:54,000
It literally makes no sense we all struggle with something completely different.
这确实说不通。每个人面对的困难完全不同。

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,280
And journaling is going to help you get to the root of what you're struggling with.
她认为，写日记能帮助你找到自己所面临困难的根源。

15
00:00:57,280 --> 00:01:02,560
So that you can then identify the steps to create from there and when it comes to journaling there's no right or wrong answer.
这样，你就能据此确定接下来要做什么。至于写日记，没有什么标准的对错答案。

16
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:08,430
I think yes it's important to use it as an emotional release when you're having a bad day when you're struggling with something when you want to rant.
她觉得，把日记当作情绪出口很重要，比如你心情不好、正在面对困难，或者想抱怨的时候。

17
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:10,561
Your journal can literally be your therapist.
她甚至把日记比作你的治疗师。

18
00:01:10,561 --> 00:01:17,641
And it's an important way to release any negative emotions you're harboring which are then kind of ruining your wellness and your mood n.
她认为，这是一种释放积压负面情绪的重要方式，因为这些情绪会影响你的状态和心情。

19
00:01:17,641 --> 00:01:19,001
So you can get it off your chest.
这样就能把心里的话说出来。

20
00:01:19,001 --> 00:01:22,001
But I also love to use journaling to document the good.
但我也喜欢通过日记记录好的事情。

21
00:01:22,001 --> 00:01:27,160
Not only for gratitude which can raise your vibration and definitely be an amazing self care practice.
她说，这不只是为了感恩；她认为感恩可以“提高振动频率”，也是很棒的自我照顾练习。

22
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:30,361
But to kind of become your own life coach.
也为了在一定程度上成为自己的生活教练。

23
00:01:30,361 --> 00:01:36,641
When you have documented enough of your life through good and bad days when writing in like a diary format in your journal.
当你已经用日记形式记录了足够多的生活，包括好日子和不好的日子时……

24
00:01:36,641 --> 00:01:42,681
When you're having a bad day you can look back and read on the days that you felt so happy and so alive and so amazing.
在难过的时候，你就能回头读自己那些特别快乐、充满活力、感觉很棒的日子。

25
00:01:42,681 --> 00:01:48,600
And then you can literally see oh I did this this and this and that's probably why I ended up having a good day.
然后你就能看到：哦，我做了这件、那件，还有另一件事，所以那天大概才过得很好。

26
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:55,361
And you literally have this bank of information as to what makes you happy not everybody else.
这样你就有了一库信息，了解什么让你自己开心，而不是别人。

27
00:01:55,361 --> 00:02:01,561
And it's literally the best self development advice you could ever get because it's from yourself based on your life experiences.
她认为，这是你能得到的最好的自我发展建议，因为它来自你自己，基于你个人的生活经历。

28
00:02:01,561 --> 00:02:05,521
This links into step number two doing favors for your future self.
这也联系到第二步：为未来的自己做点好事。

29
00:02:05,521 --> 00:02:11,590
I have read a list in my phone called things that make me feel good versus things that make me feel bad for so long.
我很长一段时间都在看手机里的一份清单，叫“让我感觉好的事”和“让我感觉不好的事”。

30
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:16,281
And this was inspired from a post I saw called energy givers versus takers.
这是受我看到的一篇帖子启发，叫作“给予能量的事与消耗能量的事”。

31
00:02:16,281 --> 00:02:20,481
And this basically show those things that will raise your happiness levels and your dopamine.
她说，这篇帖子大体列出了会提升快乐感和多巴胺的事情。

32
00:02:20,481 --> 00:02:25,071
Versus things that are going to take away from it that aren't going to benefit your self care at all.
也列出了会消耗它们、对自己的照顾没有帮助的事情。

33
00:02:25,081 --> 00:02:30,951
And I thought it's time that I do this for what benefits me and my unique needs.
我就想，是时候为适合我、符合我独特需要的事情做这样的记录了。

34
00:02:30,961 --> 00:02:33,720
So I literally just became conscious of how I felt.
所以我开始有意识地留意自己的感受。

35
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:37,041
And how I was moving through each phase of my life through each day through each week.
也留意自己怎样度过生活中的每个阶段、每一天、每一周。

36
00:02:37,041 --> 00:02:39,241
And I realized okay when I drink coffee I feel this way.
我就发现，好吧，我喝咖啡的时候，会有这种感觉。

37
00:02:39,241 --> 00:02:45,081
When I go out on a night with my friends and I drink too much I feel sadder over the weekend so that's something that makes me feel bad.
和朋友出去玩、喝太多酒以后，我周末会更难过，所以这就是一件让我感觉不好的事。

38
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:49,600
And it's important to write these things down along with with certain things that you know light you up.
把这些写下来很重要，也要写下那些你知道能让自己开心的事情。

39
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:54,481
So putting on a good outfit drinking a cup of tea in the morning having a slow morning routine.
比如穿一套好看的衣服、早上喝杯茶，还有不慌不忙的晨间日常。

40
00:02:54,481 --> 00:02:58,961
Because on those days where you feel sad and helpless and you're in this victim mentality.
因为在你感觉难过、无助，陷入她所说的“受害者心态”的那些日子……

41
00:02:58,961 --> 00:03:02,521
You are finally going to take accountability to pull yourself out of it.
你终于可以承担起责任，想办法把自己从那种状态里拉出来。

42
00:03:02,521 --> 00:03:12,270
You are finally taking responsibility over your own happiness by doing this favor today just by writing out what you know takes away your energy and what adds to your energy.
今天只要把什么消耗精力、什么增加精力写出来，就等于为自己做件好事，并对自己的快乐负责。

43
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:19,160
So on the days that you're struggling and your brain power isn't really there you have a list of things that you can do to pull yourself out of that rot.
这样，当你遇到困难、也没什么精力思考的时候，就有一份能帮自己脱离低落状态的行动清单。
